## Flutter White-Label Lending App Rules

### Architecture
- Follow Clean Architecture: data → domain → presentation layers per feature
- Never import Firebase/Dio in presentation layer — use repositories via use cases
- BLoC/Cubit for state management, go_router for navigation

### White-Label
- Never hardcode colors, strings, logos, or API URLs
- Always read from FlavorConfig.instance (lib/flavors/flavor_config.dart)

### Code Style
- Use package imports (package:local_lending_app/...), never relative across features
- Use const constructors everywhere possible
- All BLoC events and states must use @freezed
- Never use print() — use logger
- Format: dart format, Lint: flutter analyze (must be zero issues)

### Repayment Logic
- EMI calculation ONLY via EmiCalculator (lib/core/utils/emi_calculator.dart)
- Handle all 4 frequencies: daily, weekly, biweekly, monthly
- Currency: always via CurrencyFormatter.format() → "₹1,23,456"
- Monthly due dates: use month-end clamp (Jan 31 → Feb 28)

### Testing
- Every new screen → widget test + golden test
- Every new BLoC → unit test covering all states
- Minimum 80% coverage (make coverage)
- Use mocktail, never mockito
